1FPP; _Reduction to Fundamental Triangle_

(_g_2=1, \(g\)2=0)

If \(g\)2>0 and \(g\)2=0, homogeneity relations allow us to reduce our consideration of \(Q\) to \(Q\) (_z_; 1, 0) (_Q_', \(z\) and \(s\) are handled similarly). Thus \(Q\) (_z_; \(g\)2, 0) = \(g\)2